caf933f6b512c139655e3e343e3" "q-17330/selection/b948c57051e535a3ab72a3f7e2754ca228f6be199b67dfa0e474032c64b62d2c" "q-17330/selection/f0f65a35a02a8eb76c19dddf7676467dfad527beeebe76c9d27ab570959be598" "q-17330/selection/96385df8acc65983bebc8ed6b794283b54d2395a3fceb4ec4340a21b866c8769"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17330" :question/id #uuid "a7fb8fd7-85f4-5c55-8097-022bd414615d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17330" :question/problem "Simplify the expression ${[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]}^{16}.$" :question/worked-solution "For expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=16$ and $\\phi =\\frac{\\theta }{2}.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]}^{16} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(16\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-17330/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc91582-8d44-5de1-9c98-1c5de173eefb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17330"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104123/selection/186c98b42d2206a12ef9a55ea521a29d3a7b5ec370593189030c5166ed20684d" :answer/id #uuid "bf8ef90e-855a-51db-b04e-3ae4203c7f1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\theta }{3})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\theta }{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104123/selection/90618d5750348a7fc7933d31b90f68873d940c9d5ea3fdd092b2678bb1d79c4d" :answer/id #uuid "6c56a2b4-7289-5889-aed5-525ee8a4036a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104123/selection/7fe7f508bebe6fdcc9bcec8a138b987d672f039425bcaecab15fcad361f33d65" :answer/id #uuid "13eec265-fa1a-527b-8899-58b5980cdf1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\theta }{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104123/selection/de810a319cbab4bc08a56c83f1b9935d2492d6649b3570516cc19dc7a62d65ad" :answer/id #uuid "b2e89d45-82a6-5a2a-a846-f34f4193f309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104123/selection/dee5e513c5073f7247eaeb6a96573087047cf500bfd8da2ac63999d8cbf8bf22" :answer/id #uuid "b850ec25-4f57-59d7-8804-62441bd734d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104123/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fca9c05d-d7e3-545e-a5d1-3545089ebb79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104123/selection/de810a319cbab4bc08a56c83f1b9935d2492d6649b3570516cc19dc7a62d65ad" :answer-field/choices ["q-104123/selection/186c98b42d2206a12ef9a55ea521a29d3a7b5ec370593189030c5166ed20684d" "q-104123/selection/90618d5750348a7fc7933d31b90f68873d940c9d5ea3fdd092b2678bb1d79c4d" "q-104123/selection/7fe7f508bebe6fdcc9bcec8a138b987d672f039425bcaecab15fcad361f33d65" "q-104123/selection/de810a319cbab4bc08a56c83f1b9935d2492d6649b3570516cc19dc7a62d65ad" "q-104123/selection/dee5e513c5073f7247eaeb6a96573087047cf500bfd8da2ac63999d8cbf8bf22"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104123" :question/id #uuid "5fe46279-8589-565d-a925-837c7d9f7807" :question/math-academy-id "q-104123" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{3}}=[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{-3}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\phi ]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-3$ and $\\phi =5\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{3}} & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{-3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(-3)\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(-3)\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104123/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104123"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325322/field-1/4bdcabdf509f26b1d3b6ab8909d68a664be59de9be04be64e1e4d2660e560fac" :answer/id #uuid "8f2b50f4-ac77-5ed5-852c-67a6fd4947ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(10\\theta)-i\\sin(10\\theta)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325322/field-1/952884a2b4fe1b40c9877737e3289b268853242b1aa7889fb7edd63326f4bbfe" :answer/id #uuid "2e4f56e1-c178-59ae-8aa7-eb7803b760f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(10\\theta)+i\\sin(10\\theta)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325322/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "06cf9771-cdad-50c9-a09f-15a38efc2cb3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325322/field-1/4bdcabdf509f26b1d3b6ab8909d68a664be59de9be04be64e1e4d2660e560fac" :answer-field/choices ["q-325322/field-1/4bdcabdf509f26b1d3b6ab8909d68a664be59de9be04be64e1e4d2660e560fac" "q-325322/field-1/952884a2b4fe1b40c9877737e3289b268853242b1aa7889fb7edd63326f4bbfe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325322" :question/id #uuid "3c28e84b-c53e-504e-b8c2-0b7814a2c45f" :question/math-academy-id "q-325322" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}}.$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}}={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-10}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-10$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-10} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-10\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-10\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-10\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-10\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10\\theta ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-325322/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325322"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325325/field-1/fb07d3200e0b6b2e09ce4bbcf468f73b7edc98d28a200463c337d563953e189a" :answer/id #uuid "95a4f400-c75c-5613-aad7-af0f436ee8b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\cos(4\\theta)-3i\\sin(4\\theta)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325325/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5aebd88-b9d1-569f-9e98-c0ef454c7959" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325325/field-1/fb07d3200e0b6b2e09ce4bbcf468f73b7edc98d28a200463c337d563953e189a" :answer-field/choices ["q-325325/field-1/fb07d3200e0b6b2e09ce4bbcf468f73b7edc98d28a200463c337d563953e189a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325325" :question/id #uuid "56395c12-56d9-5b2e-a8bf-03ab5ebc1eb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-325325" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}},$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}}=3{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-4}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-4$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}} & =3{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-4} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-4\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-4\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\theta )]=3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-325325/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325325"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325346/field-1/9034d1dace814839087a86a6fb705fc891541f8f3ce1e627aae377caae20632e" :answer/id #uuid "daaaf824-12e2-5927-bdf3-a4bd9af7d26e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\cos(20\\theta)+4i\\sin(20\\theta)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325346/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d11956c1-8012-5219-8bf3-fd4c5f5f9e84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325346/field-1/9034d1dace814839087a86a6fb705fc891541f8f3ce1e627aae377caae20632e" :answer-field/choices ["q-325346/field-1/9034d1dace814839087a86a6fb705fc891541f8f3ce1e627aae377caae20632e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325346" :question/id #uuid "2c1e61a2-b8d6-58ca-b034-10df8d60647c" :question/math-academy-id "q-325346" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{4}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]^{5}}$ in the form $x+\\text{i}y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{4}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]^{5}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{5}} & =4{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-5$ and $\\phi =4\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{-5} & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5\\cdot 4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\cdot 4\\theta )] \\\\  & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-20\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-20\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-20\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-20\\theta )] & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta )]] \\\\  & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n4{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{-5}=4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta )].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-325346/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc91582-8d44-5de1-9c98-1c5de173eefb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325346"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
